# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on the Windows machines this is developed on, so git
# checks files out with CRLF. Python tooling and the Linux host both expect LF,
# and a shell script or Procfile that reaches Render with CRLF fails to run at
# all. Committed content was always LF; this stops the checkout rewriting it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets git must never touch. Fonts especially: the invoice PDFs are
# rendered with the bundled Bengali faces, and a .ttf that has been through
# line-ending normalisation is a font that no longer parses.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
